model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "The crash operator workflow runs only on main, one dispatch at a time, and holds the operator signing key in its single operator step. Observe sends only the read-only inspect, fleet-inspect and active-health handoff commands. Inspect and apply require the dispatch request id to equal the packet nonce and a literal coordinator GO without placeholders. The account comes from protected configuration and the worker from a read-only native release state read that must name the same account. Apply first lists every earlier run of the workflow and forces inspect when any other run, or a re-run attempt, carries the nonce; an unreadable run list refuses apply. The controller's durable nonce remains the second guard. Apply is never retried, and a lost or unknown reply fails the run as uncertain. The one-day result artifact carries the supplied inputs, a canonical packet digest, timing, the forced-inspect decision, fixed refusal text and unchanged controller results, never the signing key, signed envelopes, response headers or bridge error text."
    }
  }
}
